# .trivyignore - accepted HIGH/CRITICAL findings for freeunit-php
#
# Every entry below is a vulnerability that, at the scan date, has NO upstream
# fix available (Debian status "affected" or "fix_deferred", empty FixedVersion)
# and lives in the Debian trixie base image or the sury PHP / image-codec stack.
# None are in FreeUnit's own .deb packages, and none are resolvable by the
# `apt full-upgrade` the base_image stage already runs - there is nothing to
# upgrade to. They are acknowledged and suppressed so the scan surfaces only
# NEW, actionable (fixed) issues instead of this permanent unfixable backlog.
#
# Trivy reads this file automatically (default ./.trivyignore), so both
# `make scan` and the CI trivy step honour it with no extra flags.
#
# Durable alternative: run trivy with `--ignore-unfixed`. That auto-suppresses
# the whole unfixed class (which is 100% of the list below) and never goes
# stale, at the cost of an explicit per-CVE audit trail. This file is the
# explicit-list option; pick one, don't run both.
#
# Scanned image: freeunit-php:trixie-1.35.6-build4-php8.4
# Generated:     2026-07-10
# REVIEW BY:     2026-10-10 - re-scan and drop any CVE that upstream has since
#                fixed (a fixed CVE left here would silence a real regression).
#                New base-image CVEs are NOT covered until added here.

# --- Image codecs (pulled by the PHP `imagick` extension) ---
# Exploitable only when the app decodes UNTRUSTED images. Dropping the imagick
# extension from php_image would remove this entire cluster at the source.

